Swiss Parliaments Corpus — test split (spc-test — WER/BLEU)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Reference transcripts for the `spc-test` dataset derive from the Swiss
Parliaments Corpus (SPC), Bernese cantonal parliament: Swiss German speech
aligned to the Standard German parliamentary record. Acquired as the two test
parquet shards of `i4ds/SPC_test`, fetched by URL at a pinned revision and
sha256-verified (raven_asr/datasets/spc_test.py).

  License: MIT — INFERRED, NOT STATED BY THE DISTRIBUTION WE FETCH.
    The `i4ds/SPC_test` dataset card carries no license tag at all: the Hub API
    returns its `cardData` without a `license` key (checked 2026-09-03). We
    inherit MIT from the upstream FHNW publication that this repository
    re-releases — https://www.cs.technik.fhnw.ch/i4ds-datasets lists
    "Swiss Parliaments Corpus … License: MIT" (checked 2026-09-01).
    This is an inference from the upstream publication, not a licence grant
    read off the artefact we download. It is recorded here as an inference on
    purpose; if i4ds tags the card, replace this paragraph with the tag.
  Citation:
    Plüss et al., "Swiss Parliaments Corpus, an Automatically Aligned Swiss
    German Speech to Standard German Text Corpus", SwissText 2021.
  Source:
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/i4ds/SPC_test
    https://www.cs.technik.fhnw.ch/i4ds-datasets

Audio is fetched by the reproducer from the pinned Hub revision and never
redistributed here. Only per-utterance reference/hypothesis text would be a
Tier-1 artifact commit candidate.

