  Durability caveat, recorded because a licence is not an acquisition path:
  the only distribution we know of is a Dropbox share link. It is citable and
  checksummed — a stranger can fetch and verify the exact bytes our numbers were
  measured on — but it has no version history and no institutional commitment,
  and it can disappear without notice. Per ADR-app-0054 the link is carried as a
  tracked liability: the sha256 is verified on every acquisition so a silent
  substitution fails loudly, a durable mirror (self-hosting is permitted by MIT;
  a Zenodo deposit would add a DOI) is being pursued and is OUTSTANDING as of
  2026-09-03, and only if the link dies before that mirror exists is the
  published number marked as measured-but-no-longer-externally-reproducible.

